  "ingredients": [
    "3 cloves garlic, minced",
    "1 tablespoon dried rosemary",
    "salt and pepper to taste",
    "2 pounds boneless pork loin roast",
    "0.25 cup olive oil",
    "0.5 cup white wine"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/xCu17q1EB8IEvIF4lPUKRGhaFC0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21766-Roasted-pork-loin-step1-108-fff000262c044153a1b8ccd4d69e1d65.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21766/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crush garlic with rosemary, salt, and pepper in a mortar and pestle to make a paste. If you don’t have a mortar and pestle, mince ingredients finely and mash with the flat side of a knife.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/dig8ZM0Kvqi8YA-dHkIJ8cIU_sY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21766-Roasted-pork-loin-step2-109-6c03b5be890f42728a582e756815965e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21766/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pierce meat with a sharp knife in several places and press garlic paste into the openings. Rub pork loin with the remaining garlic mixture and olive oil. Set into a small roasting pan or oven-safe skillet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IeSms6wXFExg0KltIpy2FbC5cAo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21766-Roasted-pork-loin-step3-110-9715c4e941324ce9b3ae34229cd152e4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21766/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place pork loin into the preheated oven, turning and basting with pan liquids every 30 minutes. Cook until the pork is no longer pink in the center, 90 minutes to 2 hours. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 145 degrees F (63 degrees C). Remove roast to a platter and keep warm.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Place pan onto the stove over medium-high heat and pour wine into it. Heat wine and stir to loosen browned bits from the bottom of the pan. Simmer for 3 to 5 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/OfAXfkfDR6s1Ml61M6qY5l1OyNA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21766-Roasted-pork-loin-step4-111-fe7a75491a784b88bb9659951761ef85.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21766/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice pork loin and serve with pan juices.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
